# Flutter Core Rules

## Clean Architecture Rule
- Every feature must follow clean architecture with proper layer separation
- Maintain clear boundaries between presentation, domain, and data layers
- Use dependency injection with GetIt
- Follow repository pattern for data access
- Keep dependencies flowing inward
- Organize code in feature-based modules

## Import Convention Rule
- Always use `package:` imports for files within the `lib` directory
- Never use relative imports (e.g. `../`, `./`) for `lib` files — convert them to `package:` URIs

```dart
// ❌ BAD
import '../../core/utils/logger.dart';
import '../widgets/custom_button.dart';

// ✅ GOOD
import 'package:aimtg_mobile/core/utils/logger.dart';
import 'package:aimtg_mobile/features/auth/presentation/widgets/custom_button.dart';
```

## State Management and Performance Rule
- Use BLoC/Cubit for state management
- Keep state updates explicit via events/cubit methods and immutable states
- Avoid unnecessary widget rebuilds
- Use const constructors where applicable
- Cache network requests appropriately
- Profile performance regularly

These rules are mandatory and will be automatically enforced.

